{
  "_readme": [
    "Bible book names in Relay's tier-1 languages, keyed by the canonical English",
    "name in detection::CANONICAL_BOOKS.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS DATA AND NOT RUST:",
    "Relay's differentiator is African-language speech. Its maintainer does not",
    "speak all three of these languages fluently, and a WRONG alias does not fail",
    "safely — it puts the wrong scripture on a wall in front of a congregation.",
    "Keeping the names here means a native speaker can correct them in a one-line",
    "pull request without touching Rust, without a build, and without knowing what",
    "a HashMap is. That is the only way this table ever becomes trustworthy.",
    "",
    "MATCHING IS DIACRITIC-INSENSITIVE. 'Jòhánù', 'Johánù' and 'Johanu' all match:",
    "detection::normalize folds tone marks and dots-below before lookup, because",
    "whisper will emit all three spellings depending on the audio. Write the name",
    "properly with its diacritics — the folding is handled for you.",
    "",
    "OMISSION IS SAFE. A missing alias just means Relay does not detect that book",
    "in that language yet — the status quo. A WRONG alias means a wrong verse on",
    "the screen. So where a name was not verifiable against a real Bible-society",
    "translation, it is left out ON PURPOSE. Please add it rather than guess.",
    "",
    "Sources: Swahili — Biblia Takatifu / Neno (Biblica). Yoruba — Yoruba",
    "Contemporary Bible (Biblica). Hausa — Bible Society of Nigeria / Hausa",
    "Contemporary Bible (Biblica).",
    "",
    "STATUS: sw complete (66). yo and ha are PARTIAL and need a native speaker to",
    "finish them — see docs/LANGUAGES.md."
  ],

